// --- Orthopedic Injuries (nests inside the Trauma section) -------------------
// Tintinalli's Emergency Medicine (Section 22, chapters 267-278) was used
// only for the topic/chapter list. All HPI/Examination template wording is
// original. Every topic cites a free NCBI Bookshelf/StatPearls (NIH-hosted)
// source. CDSCO Class A: toggles insert BLANK structured fields only —
// nothing here classifies fracture severity (e.g. Gustilo-Anderson grade),
// stages a dislocation, or calculates a recommendation.

const UNIVERSAL_ORTHO_HPI = `MECHANISM OF INJURY
- Type: direct blow / axial load / angular (bending) / torque (twisting) / fall / crush / other
- Description:
- Time of injury:      Time since injury:
- Position of limb/joint at moment of injury

SYMPTOM DETAIL
- Pain: site, severity, worse with movement/weight-bearing Y/N
- Deformity noticed by patient Y/N
- Swelling onset (immediate / delayed)
- Numbness / tingling distribution
- Weakness — specific movement affected
- Able to bear weight / use the limb since injury Y/N

PREHOSPITAL COURSE
- Splinting/immobilization applied before arrival Y/N, by whom
- Reduction attempted before arrival Y/N

RELEVANT BACKGROUND
- Past fractures/surgery to same site
- Bone-health history (osteoporosis, prior pathologic fracture, steroid use)
- Occupation / dominant hand or leg
- Medications (anticoagulants)
- Allergies
- Tetanus immunization status (if open wound present)

SPECIAL CONSIDERATIONS (fill if applicable)
- Skeletally immature patient (growth plate involvement possible)
- Repetitive/overuse pattern (possible stress fracture)
- History inconsistent with injury pattern — non-accidental injury screening note`;

const UNIVERSAL_ORTHO_EXAM = `LOOK
- Deformity, angulation, shortening
- Swelling, bruising
- Skin integrity: closed / open wound (describe size, contamination — visual note only)
- Colour of the limb distal to injury

FEEL
- Point tenderness (mark site)
- Crepitus
- Skin temperature distal to injury

MOVE
- Active range of motion
- Passive range of motion (only if not contraindicated by obvious fracture)
- Pain on movement — location and character

NEUROVASCULAR STATUS (distal to injury)
- Pulses present/absent, compare both sides
- Capillary refill
- Sensation by nerve distribution
- Motor function by nerve distribution
- Compartment tenseness / pain on passive stretch — recorded as a finding only

JOINT ABOVE AND JOINT BELOW
- Examined and documented separately, even if not the primary complaint site`;

